# escape_shade_manach -- the monk, Brother Áed of Clonmacnoise, one of the dead waiting at the well. Fourteen years on
# his book, one page left to write when the fire came. Before Géaga looks away he waits as you do; after, she has let
# you go.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 8

= waiting
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
You are waiting also? Good. Then we are two, and the waiting is less strange with two.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
I have lost the count of how long. That grieves me. I was always careful with numbers.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= the book
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
I had a book. My own. Fourteen years from the first ruling of the vellum:
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
the life of the blessed Ciarán, the nature of the salmon,
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
the stars above Clonmacnoise, and what the old ones named them before Patrick came.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= one page
@when !note escape_geaga_blind_eye
The fire took the house on a Thursday.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
I had one page left to write. Fourteen years, and one page.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= she let you go
@when note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
She let you go. Yes. Yes, I see it. You are plainly a different order of thing than I am.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
I copied letters fourteen years in a cold room above a river.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= Fionnbarr
@when note escape_geaga_blind_eye
@continue
There is a young brother at Clonmacnoise, Fionnbarr. He was fond of me.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Tell him I am not suffering. It is only that I cannot settle.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= the Nail of the Sky
@when note escape_geaga_blind_eye
And if you find a pen, and a clean piece of vellum: the last star was to be the cold one, that does not move.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
The fishermen call it the Nail of the Sky, for all things turn about it and it holds firm.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
One sentence. I would feel better, knowing it was written somewhere. Go now. Go.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
